Key results: all 54 tests + size budget pass; the real-socket path was verified live end-to-end (4000/4001 rejects, shared goAt, finish order, DNF settle); three real defects were found and reproduced — a hard crash in smokeClient (undeclared `id` in an ES module, exact stack captured), its hardcoded port 8080 conflicting with the documented 807x procedure, and the main.mjs port-argument parsing bug (bare `8070` bound 8080); plus two state-machine holes confirmed with FakeNet probes (stuck `racing` when all players DNF before any finish; contradictory `finishInfo` after the 30 s-forced results).

